    "## 2. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2.1 Structural Characteristics\n",
    "The dataset is entirely continuous and numerical. No missing values remain following the initial sanitation step. \n",
    "\n",
    "### 2.2 Distributional Properties (Skewness and Kurtosis)\n",
    "Astronomical parameters commonly follow power-law or log-normal distributions rather than Gaussian curves:\n",
    "* **Transit Depth (`koi_depth`) & Insolation (`koi_insol`):** Exhibit severe positive skewness ($\\gamma_1 \\gg 3$) and heavy kurtosis ($\\gamma_2 \\gg 10$), driven by rare deep eclipses and close-in stellar irradiation.\n",
    "* **Impact Parameter (`koi_impact`):** Nearly uniform across $[0, 1)$ for central crossings, with an extended tail for grazing configurations.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2.3 Outlier Exploration & Real-World Artifacts\n",
    "* **Heavy Tails:** Giant gas exoplanets and long-period bodies populate the high-variance tails.\n",
    "* **Measurement Artifacts:** Eclipsing binary star systems contaminate the sample with unphysically large transit depths ($>100,000$ ppm).\n",
    "* **Instrumental Noise:** Rolling band noise in Kepler detectors occasionally manifests as false-positive transits with marginal durations."
